As required by section 4(b) of the Apache License, the following are the
significant changes made to the original work:

  - Express 4 compatibility removed; the project targets Express 5 only.
  - Source converted to TypeScript with strict type checking.
  - Router dispatch reworked so a chain of N middlewares allocates one promise
    instead of N, and the mount stack is no longer walked on every hop.
  - Request bodies are collected into a single buffer instead of being copied
    once per chunk and again on concatenation.
  - Empty request bodies now produce the same value each Express body parser
    produces, rather than being skipped.
  - Benchmark harness reworked: NODE_ENV is set, wrk errors and response
    validation are no longer discarded, rows bounded by shared work are
    labelled, and scenarios were added for request shapes that were not covered.
  - Linting, formatting and commit hooks added.

